  "means": {
    "overview": "The rebate did what rebates do: people brought installations forward. April 2026 was the last full month of the richer discount, and May was much quieter. The national count here is certificates already approved, not the higher figure ministers quoted in November, which includes batteries still waiting to be processed.",
    "where": "South Australia has the most batteries for the number of homes counted in 2021. Tasmania and the Northern Territory have the fewest. New South Wales has the largest number of batteries, because it has the most homes, not because uptake is the most intense. Western Australia and the Northern Territory are not in the east-coast wholesale market, so this page does not price a battery there.",
    "payback": "These years count only the money from charging when wholesale power is cheap and discharging when it is expensive. They do not count storing a household's own rooftop solar, which is often the larger saving, or any network payment. On that wholesale-only view, South Australia is the only region close to a 10-year warranty. The next scheduled cut in the discount, from January 2027, adds about 0.6 years in South Australia. It does not change which region pays back fastest.",
    "prices": "In South Australia the cheapest two midday hours averaged about $-8 per megawatt-hour over the year, so a battery was often paid to charge. About 29% of South Australian intervals had a negative price, against 5% in Tasmania. That gap, not the number of batteries, is why a South Australian battery earns more from price swings.",
    "action": "A household should not buy a battery on wholesale swings alone unless they are in South Australia and happy with a payback near the warranty. Ask the installer for the price after the federal discount, and treat quotes that assume two full cycles every day as optimistic. A retailer with customers in South Australia or Victoria is sitting on the most negative midday prices. A government cutting the discount further will slow installations, as May 2026 already showed, and will lengthen wholesale payback most where the price swings are smallest."
  },
